FILE: vUX-cShapes.js
FEATURE: border-color-cycle
DATE: 2026-10-11
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'cshapes-rectangle-fixes' (uncommitted at the time)

REASON
vilshub.com fades its contact-form border through five colours, 2s per colour, by tweening
config.lineColor. animatedRectangle() read lineColor only at the start of each cycle (every
duration ms), so a mid-cycle change waited up to a full cycle and a tween could not show. The
strokeStyle is now set every frame from the current value, like lineWidth already was.

OLD_SECTION
                function startCycle() {
                    ...
                    canObj.setLineDash(ARsegment);
                    canObj.strokeStyle = ARlinecolor;
                    ...
                function frame() {
                    ...
                    canObj.lineDashOffset = (ARclockWise ? -1 : 1) * progress * distance;
                    canObj.clearRect(0, 0, size.width, size.height);

NEW_SECTION
                function startCycle() {
                    ...
                    canObj.setLineDash(ARsegment);
                    ...
                function frame() {
                    ...
                    canObj.lineDashOffset = (ARclockWise ? -1 : 1) * progress * distance;
                    //read every frame, like lineWidth, so config.lineColor can be changed (or tweened)
                    //while the rectangle runs and shows on the next frame, not the next cycle
                    canObj.strokeStyle = ARlinecolor;
                    canObj.clearRect(0, 0, size.width, size.height);
